{% if 'how_to_work_full' in s %}

### How to work in this repo

- **Trust the index.** `verified: true` and `_meta.complete` mean the bytes were checked against the live tree, so never re-read them. Re-read only what `bounds: "approximate"` names. When `_meta.stale_warning` is set, Read the files that response served. After a batch of uncommitted edits, `repowise update --working-tree` refreshes the index. `confidence` rates the prose, not the evidence: on `low` read the top evidence row or the `candidate_files` the reply names. `index_behind: true` alone is informational.
{% if data.keyless %}
- **No model on this index.** `get_answer` replies are low confidence by design, so open its top `best_guesses` / `candidate_files` rows; `search_codebase` is full-text only, so `[fts]` hits are normal. The user adds a model with a provider key and `{{ data.model_command }}`; suggest it, do not run it.
{% endif %}
- **A zero carries its basis.** An empty `callers`/`callees`/`used_by` comes with a `*_basis` saying how much of that language's calls the graph resolved, so read it before concluding nothing calls a symbol. On `get_answer`, `_meta.scope_hint` names the areas the answer did not touch.
- **Pre-edit, not instead-of-edit.** These tools decide *which* files to read and edit. {{ read_note }}
{{ checks }}
- **Noisy commands** (tests, builds, `git log`/`diff`, searches, listings): prefer `repowise distill <cmd>`, the same command with its exit code preserved and errors-first output. A `[repowise#<ref>: N lines omitted]` marker is recoverable via `repowise expand <ref>` (add `-q <regex>` to filter); never re-run the command to see omitted output.
- **Recording a decision** you had to reason out: `repowise decision add --agent <your slug> --title T --decision D --rationale '<why, what you rejected>' --affects <path> --evidence-commit <sha>` records it without prompting and prints the id (`--format json` to parse it back); the slug names you, e.g. `claude_code`. It lands as a candidate for review and never governs until accepted. You may review and accept candidates: `repowise decision candidates` lists what each still needs, `repowise decision confirm <id> --agent <your slug>` accepts one (add `--reason`, `--scope`, `--evidence` or `--decision` for a missing part), and `dismiss`, `merge` and `deprecate` take `--agent` too. Acceptances are signed as yours; a repository with agent acceptance off refuses them.
